<Project>

  <!--
    Avalonia ships a build-time telemetry collector (the Avalonia.BuildServices package, a
    transitive dependency of Avalonia itself). Its AvaloniaStats target runs before
    CoreCompile and posts anonymised build metadata - hashed project and machine name, a
    machine GUID, OS, Avalonia version, IDE - to Avalonia's servers.

    It is build-time only and collects no source, no file paths and nothing from a running
    app, so it never sees a dataset or a trained adapter. It is disabled here anyway,
    because this project is offline by design: loralei itself opens no connection outside
    `models pull`, and a build of its GUI should not either.

    Avalonia's documented opt-out is the AVALONIA_TELEMETRY_OPTOUT=1 environment variable,
    which depends on every shell and IDE that ever builds this remembering to set it.
    Overriding the target makes it a property of the repository instead. Setting the
    environment variable as well does no harm.

    If an Avalonia upgrade renames this target, the override silently stops applying - so
    the check is `cd gui && dotnet build -t:Rebuild` under strace, expecting no outbound
    connection. See README.md, "Privacy".
  -->
  <Target Name="AvaloniaStats" />

</Project>
